---
kind: scene
id: shop.evening
title: Evenings at the workbench
on: slotStart
when: '@night && run.day < 5'
once: false
---

## The workbench

::bg{location="lantern_shop" time="night"}
::music{playback="start" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
::actor{character="pell" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
::set{run.seen.pell = run.day}

<match subject="run.lantern.frame">
  <when is="true">
    @narrator{code="0010"}: The reed frame sits on the workbench, curved like a ribcage.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator{code="0020"}: The workbench is bare except for a pot of glue and Pell's reading glasses.
    @pell{code="0010" emotion="teasing"}: No frame yet? Theo Maddox is at the pier every morning. He doesn't bite. Much.
  </otherwise>
</match>

<match subject="run.lantern.paper">
  <when is="true">
    @narrator{code="0030"}: Beside it, the kozo sheets, weighted flat under a dictionary.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @pell{code="0020"}: And paper. Ines at the library. Afternoons.
  </otherwise>
</match>

<match subject="run.lantern.wish">
  <when is="unset" test="@lanternDone">
    @narrator{code="0040"}: The paper is on. It is, unmistakably, a lantern — lopsided at the seam, but a lantern.
    @pell{code="0030" emotion="happy"}: Every lantern gets a wish on the inside of the paper. Where the candle can read it.
    @pell{code="0040"}: Go on. I won't look. I'll look a bit.
    <branch id="wish" prompt="Pell holds out the brush.">
      <choice id="sea" text="Something for the sea." into="run.lantern.wish" value="sea">
        @sol{code="0010" mono}: Keep them safe. Whoever's out there tonight.
      </choice>
      <choice id="home" text="Something for home." into="run.lantern.wish" value="home">
        @sol{code="0020" mono}: Let the shop stay open one more year.
      </choice>
      <choice id="someone" text="Something for someone." into="run.lantern.wish" value="someone">
        @sol{code="0030" mono}: I'm not writing their name. The lantern will know.
        @pell{code="0050" emotion="teasing"}: I didn't see a thing.
      </choice>
      <choice id="later" text="Not tonight.">
        @pell{code="0060"}: It'll keep. Wishes do.
      </choice>
    </branch>
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @pell{code="0070" when="has(run.lantern.wish)"}: Don't read your wish back. It's bad luck. I made that up, but still.
  </otherwise>
</match>

@pell{code="0080"}: Bed, then. Tomorrow's another day of this.

::actor{character="pell" action="fadeOut"}
::music{playback="fadeOut"}
